 This week we've been busy sorting apples at our small orchard. As we've been through the bins, the sun has been shining, the breeze has been blowing, and the apples have been gathering in the bins waiting to be either sold at market or used for home consumption. It's a job that requires patience, persistence, and a keen eye for detail.
To start, we've been careful to remove any unwanted items from the bins, such as leaves, twigs, and other debris. This ensures that only the best apples are being sorted. We've then weighed each apple to determine its size and quality. The smaller apples are sorted into one bin while the larger apples are sorted into another.
As we've been through the bins, we've noticed that the different batches of apples have distinct characteristics. Some are more tart, while others are sweeter. Some have a softer skin, while others are firmer. We've also noticed that some of the apples are starting to show signs of ripening, with slight soft spots and